# Phase-4 replay archive — pickup idempotency: a duplicated pickup report
# (Steam reliable retransmission style, injected with the dup fault) must NOT
# come back as a reject — a rejection would roll the winner's own successful
# transfer back (the item left the world table at the transfer, so the
# retransmit looks like an unknown item without the guard).
#
# Fossil of: ItemRaceTests.DuplicatedPickupReport_IsIdempotent_NoRejectToTheWinner
#            (the race probe that found the bug live)
# Fix: the reject branch also consults the transfer table — a pickup report
#      for an item the sender ALREADY owns is silent (ItemService.cs:325-333,
#      the spawn/drop idempotency family completed)

@0 spawn g1 42 test_item 1.0
@33 expect host_table 42 within 500
@33 fault g1 host dup
@33 pickup g1 42 test_item 1.0
@66 expect_no_reject g1
@66 expect no_host_table 42 within 500
